# WebUI Tailwind

- Style with **Tailwind utility classes** in JSX. Prefer existing design tokens / CSS variables already used in the app (`hsl(var(--…))`, `bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.).
- Compose conditional classes with **`cn()`** from `@/lib/utils` (clsx + tailwind-merge). Do not hand-roll string concatenation for class lists.
- Prefer extending `components/ui` primitives (and `class-variance-authority` variants there) over one-off styled `<div>` chrome when building controls.
- Avoid new CSS modules / large custom stylesheets unless Tailwind cannot express the need (e.g. third-party widget overrides).
- Avoid inline `style={{}}` for colors/spacing that Tailwind already covers; inline styles are OK for dynamic measured values (width from layout, CSS variables set at runtime).

```tsx
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// ❌ BAD
<div className={"row " + (active ? "bg-muted" : "")} style={{ marginTop: 12 }} />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className={cn("flex items-center gap-2 mt-3", active && "bg-muted/30")} />
```
